<title>UK: Copper nudging higher during LME PM, still slow.</title>
<headline>Copper nudging higher during LME PM, still slow.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER  - Edges up above  $2,490, but still range-bound. Cash/threes backwardation widens to around $70.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM  - Steadier above $1,600, testing resistance.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Stuck around  $7,300 level.</p>
<p>ZINC/LEAD - Both continue to drift.</p>
<p>TIN - Sagging, with contango relaxing once more. ALLOY - Quiet.</p>
</text>
